%h1 Add a track

%p.mb-8
  This adds a track from its repo in the exercism GitHub organisation, such as
  #{link_to 'exercism/common-lisp', 'https://github.com/exercism/common-lisp'}.
  The website reads the track's config.json, syncs its exercises and creates its forum category.
%p.mb-24
  The track will be live only if its config.json sets it as active.
  Until then, only its maintainers and maintainer admins can see it.

= form_with(url: admin_tracks_path, method: :post, class: "c-admin-form mb-40") do |form|
  - if @error
    .c-flash.mb-24
      .--errors
        = @error
        - if @existing_track
          = link_to "View the track", Exercism::Routes.track_path(@existing_track)

  .field
    = form.label :slug, "Track slug"
    = form.text_field :slug, value: @slug, placeholder: "common-lisp", autocomplete: "off", spellcheck: false
    .hint The name of the track's repo, in lowercase.

  .actions
    = form.submit "Add track", class: "btn-primary btn-m"

%h2 Recently added tracks
- if @recent_tracks.empty?
  .c-admin-empty No tracks have been added yet.
- else
  %table.c-admin-table
    %thead
      %tr
        %th Track
        %th Slug
        %th Status
        %th Added
    %tbody
      - @recent_tracks.each do |track|
        %tr
          %td= link_to track.title, Exercism::Routes.track_path(track)
          %td= track.slug
          %td= track.active? ? "Active" : "Inactive"
          %td #{time_ago_in_words(track.created_at)} ago
